{"book":46,"chapter":8,"context":{"chapter":8,"title":"Food Offered to Idols","summary":"Paul agrees that idols are nothing and there is only one God, but warns that knowledge without love can destroy a fellow believer whose conscience is weak.","background":"Much meat sold in Greek and Roman cities came from animals sacrificed at temples, and temples had dining rooms used for banquets and celebrations; such rooms have been excavated at Corinth. For new believers who had worshiped idols, eating there could feel like returning to their old gods. Others reasoned that since idols are not real, the food does not matter.","customs":[{"term":"Eating in an idol's temple","verses":"8:10","note":"Temple dining halls hosted weddings, birthdays and trade-guild dinners. Refusing to attend could cost a believer social and business connections."}],"watchFor":["'Knowledge puffeth up, but charity edifieth' (v. 1).","An early confession of one God and one Lord, echoing Israel's Shema (v. 6).","The concern for 'the weak brother… for whom Christ died' (v. 11)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 6:4","Romans 14:13-21","Acts 15:29"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Περὶ","Peri","G4012","PREP","Concerning"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","now"],["τῶν","tōn","G3588","T-GPN","the"],["εἰδωλοθύτων","eidōlothutōn","G1494","A-GPN","idol-sacrifices"],["οἴδαμεν","oidamen","G6063","V-RAI-1P","we know"],["ὅτι","hoti","G3754","CONJ","indeed"],["πάντες","pantes","G3956","A-NPM","all"],["γνῶσιν","gnōsin","G1108","N-ASF","knowledge"],["ἔχομεν","echomen","G2192","V-PAI-1P","we have"],["ἡ","hē","G3588","T-NSF","<the>"],["γνῶσις","gnōsis","G1108","N-NSF","Knowledge"],["φυσιοῖ","phusioi","G5448","V-PAI-3S","puffs up"],["ἡ","hē","G3588","T-NSF","<the>"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","but"],["ἀγάπη","agapē","G26","N-NSF","love"],["οἰκοδομεῖ","oikodomei","G3618","V-PAI-3S","builds up"]],"x":[[46008007,46008007,11],[23005021,23005021,10],[45014003,45014003,8],[46008004,46008004,6],[66002014,66002014,5],[45015014,45015014,4],[4600800